<article class="env-lemma" id="08U2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08U2">Lemma <span data-tag="08U2">20.37.8</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $E \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Assume there exist a function $p(-) : \mathbf{Z} \to \mathbf{Z}$ and a set $\mathcal{B}$ of opens of $X$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
every open in $X$ has a covering whose members are elements of $\mathcal{B}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^ p(U, H^{m - p}(E)) = 0$ for $p > p(m)$ and $U \in \mathcal{B}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the map $E \to R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits \tau _{\geq -n} E$ of Derived Categories, Remark <a href="/tag/0H72" data-tag="0H72">13.34.5</a> is an isomorphism in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0D62" data-tag="0D62">20.37.6</a> with $p(x, m) = p(m)$ and $\mathfrak {U}_ x = \{ U \in \mathcal{B} \mid x \in U\} $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>